      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A rare case of telangiectatic communication between the conal branch of the left coronary artery and the pulmonary trunk in a 50-year-old woman is reported. Unusual features included the presence of clear-cut angina on effort, unstable auscultatory findings and a RSR' pattern in lead V1, probably related to concommitant diffuse coronary atherosclerosis. Ten previously reported cases of the condition are briefly reviewed."},
